   "html_text": "Formally, matrix mechanics remains close to classical mechanics. The central idea is that all physical quantities must be represented by infinite self-adjoint matrices (later identified with operators on a Hilbert space). It is postulated that the matrices ⟦M⟧ and ⟦M⟧ representing the canonical position and momentum variables of a particle satisfy the so-called canonical commutation rule",
